# API Rules

## Auth middleware split (routes/index.ts)
- `requireAnySession` — local or tenant sessions (state, schedule, symptoms, gemini, smarthome, intercom, health-assessment)
- `requireLocalSession` — local only (scripts, haldol, health-assessment, shopper)

## Adding an endpoint
1. Add path + operationId to `lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml`
2. Add handler in `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/<domain>.ts`
3. Register router in `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/index.ts`
4. `pnpm --filter @workspace/api-spec run codegen`
5. `pnpm run typecheck`

## Gemini SSE route
`sendGeminiMessage` returns `text/event-stream` — never add JSON content-type expectations.

## Hermes dispatch (artifacts/api-server/src/lib/hermes.ts)
Single `dispatch(action, sessionId)` function. Actions dispatched via Promise.allSettled — one failure never blocks others. Never throws on malformed action, only logs warning.

Action types: ADD_EVENT, TOGGLE_SMART_DEVICE, ADD_TASK, MED_CONFIRMED, MED_REFUSED, WELLBEING_ALERT

## DB schema (lib/db/src/schema/index.ts)
19 tables. Key ones: app_state (single row), schedule_tasks, symptom_logs, voice_scripts, haldol_cycle, conversations, messages, health_questions, call_sessions, health_data_points, smart_home_devices, intercom_messages, meals, grocery_carts.
